## Constraints

- Every level (L1–L5) gets a verdict. Do not skip levels.
- The floor is defined by the known failure modes — if you discover a failure mode not in the list above, add it and note the discovery.
- The ceiling is a heuristic, not a hard line. Flag above-ceiling levels but do not auto-remove constraints — the operator decides.
- Maturity reclassifications are recommendations, not actions. The operator decides whether to reclassify or wire enforcement.
- Do not execute arbitrary Python code in Jinja2 expressions (sandboxed execution).
- Handle missing variables gracefully (leave as is or use default if specified).
